From: deCodeUx <t@t>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:41:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(evidence): diagnostic producer/validator with comparable
 archive extraction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Create packages/orchestration/diagnostic_comparison.py with typed
producer and validator for the diagnostic broad-run comparison. The
producer accepts pre-collected failure node IDs from both commits,
sorts and deduplicates them, computes SHA-256 hashes of each failure
set, and derives failure_sets_equal and set differences — no field is
caller-asserted.

The validator recomputes every derived field independently: SHA-256
hashes, sortedness, duplicate detection, count consistency,
failure_sets_equal, and set differences. Schema version 2.0.0.

23 contract tests cover: producer output always validates, invalid
inputs rejected, every tampered field detected (sha256, sortedness,
duplicates, counts, set equality, set differences, schema version,
head commit, missing keys).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
